in liposuction: An analysis of 53 consecutive patients</article-title><source>Plast Reconstr Surg</source><year>1998</year><volume>102</volume><fpage>2220</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9811024</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00006534-199811000-00063</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maxwell</surname><given-names>GP</given-names></name><name><surname>Gingrass</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ultrasound-assisted lipoplasty: A clinical study of 250 consecutive patients</article-title><source>Plast Reconstr Surg</source><year>1998</year><volume>101</volume><fpage>189</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9427937</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00006534-199801000-00034</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rohrich</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Beran</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Fodor</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The role of subcutaneous infiltration in suction-assisted lipoplasty: a review</article-title><source>Plast Reconstr Surg</source><year>1997</year><volume>99</volume><fpage>514</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9030162</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00006534-199702000-00031</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Commons</surname><given-names>GW</given-names></name><name><surname>Halperin</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Large-volume liposuction: A review of 631 consecutive cases over 12 years</article-title><source>Plast Reconstr Surg</source><year>2001</year><volume>108</volume><fpage>1753</fpage><comment>discu